n initialization script into our  shell environment that takes care of all  of this for us so we're ready to go  once this is all done let's set to the  config repo clone directory then let's  use the integrated editor to quickly  edit our mesh policy so we can tighten  up our restrictions by getting rid of  permissive mode and by requiring mutual  TLS for all matching house after we make  these configuration changes we'll run  the most vet to ensure there aren't any  other issues once we push our changes to  the upstream repository with git Anthes  config management we'll quickly detect  and apply the changes to our clusters  we'll run a little function helper to go  ahead and watch for those changes here  and that's how easy it is to apply a  policy and have anthos config management  synchronize it across all the clusters  in your environment finally we can  return to the connected services view  and after enough time passes for the  desired time span we can visually  confirm that we only had MPLS traffic  with the green locks four connected  services there are plenty of examples of  security guard rails you can set to  protect your application environment  with anthos start with a tutorial and  check out the docs to learn more we just  taken a short tour of anthos using a  sample deployment this is just a taste  of things for you to try so check out  our tutorial launch a sample deployment  and explore anthos for yourself  [Music]

